# Line endings.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. For most files
# that is harmless. For these it is not, and the failure is remote from the cause:
#
#   *.sh   a shell script with CRLF endings dies with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M"
#          on Linux and in CI. It works fine on the machine that committed it, which is what
#          makes it expensive to diagnose.
#   Dockerfile, *.bash, gradlew — same class of problem.
#   *.pem, *.ttf and other binaries must never be line-ending-translated at all.
#
# `* text=auto` keeps normal source normalised to LF in the repository while still checking out
# CRLF on Windows where that is wanted.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
gradlew     text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch the bytes.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.jks   binary
*.keystore binary
*.apk   binary
*.aab   binary
*.pem   binary
